{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1090,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a famous scene in the Lord of the\nRings where the elf Legolas claims to be able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5300,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to count the exact number of horsemen 5 leagues\naway, and on top of that can tell that their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9790,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leader is very tall. But even with the most\nperfect eyes possible, would anyone be able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14670,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see that far?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16189,
    "dDurationMs": 3741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we see, we're looking at light that's\ntraveled outwards from a light source, bounced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19930,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off an object, passed through the lens in\nthe eye, and been focused into an image on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23390,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the retina. Except... light isn't a particle\ntraveling in perfectly straight lines - it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27949,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a wave. And therein lies the problem, both\nfor us, and for Legolas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32669,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because any wave - whether water, sound or\nlight - that travels through a small opening"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36980,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will become spread out by a process known\nas diffraction, which for light, essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41100,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blurs the image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42280,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see this with a telephoto camera lens\nwhere the camera aperture has been made very"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45940,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very small - small details in the photograph\nstart to become spread out, blurred, and even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50260,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "indistinguishable! Or, if you hold the edge\nof a piece of paper in front of your eye and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54160,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "try to read past it, small words will become\nblurry!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58170,
    "dDurationMs": 4209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The blur that a small point of light spreads\nout to become is called an Airy disk, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62379,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the size of the Airy disk for distant tiny\nobjects depends only on the wavelength of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66969,
    "dDurationMs": 4051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light in question and the size of the opening\nyou're looking through. So for visible sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71020,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a human-sized pupil, diffraction limits\nus to at best be able to distinguish objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75549,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are bigger than seven one-thousandths\nof a degree, for example, an object one centimeter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79770,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in size a hundred meters away,. Another way\nof putting this is that everything 100m away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84340,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and smaller than 1cm gets blurred so that\nit appears to be about 1cm in size, no matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89130,
    "dDurationMs": 5219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how small it really is - subtle details smaller\nthan 1cm blur away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94349,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when Legolas, who has very human-sized\npupils, looked at the riders of Rohan 24 km"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99959,
    "dDurationMs": 4131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away, diffraction tells us that everything\nsmaller than 3 METERS would have been blurred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104090,
    "dDurationMs": 4379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to about three meters in size - perhaps he\ncould still count the number of horsemen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108469,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he definitely couldn't distinguish their\nheights to within a few centimeters..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111919,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unless Legolas could see in ultraviolet. Shorter\nwavelength light diffracts less, so if he"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117479,
    "dDurationMs": 5151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could see in the extreme UV, then he'd be\nable to distinguish objects 10 cm in size,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122630,
    "dDurationMs": 2919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost enough to discern the height of a man."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125549,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except that pretty much any kind of air absorbs\nextreme UV light - so even if he could see"
    } ]
  } ]
}
